meta {
  name: Extend house captain
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student-assignments/{{houseCaptainAssignmentId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "valid_to": "2027-03-31",
    "is_primary": true
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.is_primary: eq true
  res.body.role_type: eq house_captain
  res.body.section_id: isUndefined
}

docs {
  role_type is deliberately not in the body. student_assignments and
  teacher_assignments have identical shapes, and sending a teacher role here
  is refused rather than stored -- 09/09 proves that on create, and the same
  check runs on update. Leaving the field out is the ordinary case: a term
  being extended is not a change of role.

  section_id stays null. The captaincy answers to a house, not to one section,
  and a null here is what the school_wide filter keys on.
}
